        "##  {background-iframe=\"https://player.vimeo.com/video/916622482\" data-menu-title=\"Introduction to queues\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "## Data structure: Queue\n",
        "\n",
        "To orchestrate the fill, we'll use a data structure called a *queue*.\n",
        "\n",
        "![](/images/penguins.jpg){fig-alt=\"A line of penguins stretches across an ice floe and they jump from its edge into the ocean.\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "Queue:\n",
        "\n",
        "`enqueue(k)`: Places data `k` onto the structure at the end\n",
        "\n",
        "`dequeue()`: Removes and returns the \"first\" element from the structure\n",
        "\n",
        "::: notes\n",
        "-   Programmatic manifestation of standing in a service line.\n",
        "-   First in, First Out\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "# Class demo: Motivating queues\n",
        "\n",
        "## In Python: `Collections.deque`\n",
        "\n",
        "Pronounced \"deck\"\n",
        "\n",
        "![[From GeeksforGeeks: Deque in Python](https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/deque-in-python/)](https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250701150127717176/Deque.webp){fig-alt=\"A deque is a row of elements and allows to add and remove elements at both ends.\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "## Documentation\n",
        "\n",
        "```{pyodide}\n",
        "from collections import deque\n",
